ice other than percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) prior to stent placement (e.g. but not limited to, directional coronary atherectomy, excimer laser, rotational atherectomy, etc.).\"\n                  },\n                  \"right\": {\n                    \"OR\": {\n                      \"left\": {\n                        \"rawtext\": \"19. Any lesion that is located in a saphenous vein graft, however, lesions located within the native vessel but accessed through the graft are eligible.\"\n                  }\n                    }\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"right\": {\n              \"AND\": {\n                \"OR\": {\n                  \"left\": {\n                    \"rawtext\": \"20. The target vessel is in a \"last remaining\" epicardial vessel (e.g. greater than 2 non-target epicardial vessels and the bypass grafts to these territories [if present] are totally occluded).\"\n                  }\n                    }\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"right\": {\n              \"AND\": {\n                \"OR\": {\n                  \"left\": {\n                    \"rawtext\": \"21. The target lesion is located in a vessel that is not amenable to treatment with a drug-eluting stent.\"\n                  }\n                    }\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"right\": {\n              \"AND\": {\n                \"OR\": {\n                  \"left\": {\n                    \"rawtext\": \"22. The target lesion is located in a vessel that is not amenable to treatment with a bare metal stent.\"\n                  }\n                    }\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"right\": {\n              \"AND\": {\n                \"OR\": {\n                  \"left\": {\n                    \"rawtext\": \"23. The target lesion is located in a vessel that is not amenable to treatment with a bioresorbable sc